{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3474-favorite-compacts-conspiracies","id":3474,"title":"Favorite Compacts/Conspiracies?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T07:24:33-08:00","id":3474,"title":"Favorite Compacts/Conspiracies?","content":"What are everyone's favorite Compacts and Conspiracies? <br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of the VASCU; they open up X-Files -style chronicles and their Endowment is great. I also love hunters in an official context, rather than as a shady cult or top secret black ops task force. It's also an excuse to make PCs follow the law and not shoot everything on sight; they're bound by law, and could lose their jobs if they screw up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T08:07:17-08:00","id":3492,"title":"","content":"My personal favorite is the Aegis Kai Doru, just because for me personally its easiest to work them into pretty much any game (my group is always big on their magic toys).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T13:03:23-08:00","id":3704,"title":"","content":"The Ascending Ones - I love their blend of different elements; alchemy, monotheism and drug culture. I love the idea of &quot;inner city nobodies&quot; secretly having ancient knowledge and power. I do think they need a bit more on how their command structure works. (I like to think of them as lots of smallish 10 - 100 people organisations, drug rings, secret societies etc who's leaders meet up regularly in Thoth's palace and elect a ruling council from their numbers. Thoth himself isn't really involved with the AO; though he does sometimes her petitions from his worshippers in the Conspiracy. Rather he's paid rent, the rates are extortionate but a god's palace is one of the safest places in existence)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:27:03-08:00","id":4003,"title":"","content":"Well my two favorites are the ones that straddle the line between hunter and monster: Lucifuge and the Cheiron Group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T03:25:08-08:00","id":4185,"title":"","content":"Among the compacts- Ashwood Abbey (I like their hellfire club atmosphere) and Keepers of the Source (crazy hipsters :P)<br /> <br /> Among the Conspiracies- Lucifuge (&quot;I have demonic blood in me veins!) and Knights of st George (I love their templet like atmosphere)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T06:28:01-08:00","id":4257,"title":"","content":"Kings Raven (or anyone else); care to sell me on the Ascending Ones?<br /> <br /> They've always been my least favorite Conspiracy by far (excluding the Les Mysteres, but they aren't core). It strikes me as the Ascending Ones are this vaguely-defined, disorganized bunch of cobbled-together mythologies that somehow motivates them to become Hunters, and a sort of tacked-on &quot;and they also peddle smack to the inner cities.&quot; The Ageis Kai Doru has them beat for that 'ancient conspiracy' vibe, and they seem to lack a compelling motivation beyond the basic Hunter goals. <br /> <br /> I'd go so far as to wish that they'd be cut in favor of, say, the VASCU being thrown into core, but time and time again people list them as their favorite of the conspiracies. Is this like Forsaken being one of the most popular gamelines, where I'm just not a fan of something good, or am I missing something vital?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:18:41-08:00","id":4287,"title":"","content":"I think it falls to the Lucifuge because I am into all that &quot;EVIL HERITAGE BUT I TRY TO DO GOOD!&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I also really like the idea of the Cheiron Group as big business mixing it up as a Conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:31:30-08:00","id":4300,"title":"","content":"Cheiron, VALKYRIE, and VASCU are my triumvirate. I like the more modern, X-Files style conspiracies over the sort of &quot;ancient whatsits&quot; any day.<br /> <br /> The federal government knows about the supernatural, but hides it from the people. The organizations it appoints are underfunded and understaffed; is this intentional? Who knows just how compromised the entire structure is; how high does it go? Big business is in on it, and they'll do anything in the name of profit.<br /> <br /> I still dream of doing a game where VASCU and VALKYRIE reluctantly work together (the fact that they know about each other, and sometimes interact, is one of my favorite bits of canon) and are funded by Cheiron, rather than vampires. Maybe throw in Division Six. Play up the &quot;you can't trust your superiors&quot; angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:25:03-08:00","id":4340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3474-favorite-compacts-conspiracies?p=4300#post4300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cheiron, VALKYRIE, and VASCU are my triumvirate. I like the more modern, X-Files style conspiracies over the sort of &quot;ancient whatsits&quot; any day.<br /> <br /> The federal government knows about the supernatural, but hides it from the people. The organizations it appoints are underfunded and understaffed; is this intentional? Who knows just how compromised the entire structure is; how high does it go? Big business is in on it, and they'll do anything in the name of profit.<br /> <br /> I still dream of doing a game where VASCU and VALKYRIE reluctantly work together (the fact that they know about each other, and sometimes interact, is one of my favorite bits of canon) and are funded by Cheiron, rather than vampires. Maybe throw in Division Six. Play up the &quot;you can't trust your superiors&quot; angle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm invisioning Agent Mulder of VASCU explaining his conspiracy theories to Colonel Jack O'Neill of Taskforce VALKYRIE... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:33:49-08:00","id":4346,"title":"","content":"You're right on the ticket!<br /> <br /> Maybe mix things up a little tiny bit; bring the Panopticon that Division Six answers to as the shadowy superiors that both VASCU and VALKYRIE answer to, while Cheiron are private funding that sometimes request that the monsters be brought in alive, much to the consternation of the unfortunate field agents. A cold,chock-full-of-Thaumatechnology handler would be great for freaking out the poor VASCU/VALKYRIE agents, and make for a great party dynamic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:35:04-08:00","id":4349,"title":"","content":"I am the first to admit that the Ascending Ones have flaws in how they\u2019re presented \u2013 though unlike some groups *cough* TF:V Vampires *cough* I don\u2019t have any major problems with anything written. They just need some more text.<br /> <br /> The thing about the Ascending Ones is that they really are three different organisations in one. This means that each of the three have relatively less text compared to The Lcuifuge (who are very much one organisation).<br /> <br /> <br /> If you look at them as one you\u2019ll get a bit of a mess. Imagine one guy believing some weird blend of Islam and Kemetism who hunts monsters for generic reasons like religion and protecting his community; and he sells smack on the side. That\u2019s a mess.<br /> <br /> However if you look at them as three individual groups, they\u2019re look much cleaner.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Knife of Paradise don\u2019t have a cobbled together mythology, they\u2019re monotheists plain and simple. What\u2019s more they\u2019re assassins and diplomats (the two always were tied together). That\u2019s actually a pretty cool theme. If their motives are a little generic, so are quite a few other orgs. Some groups defined themselves by method, others by motive. Nothing wrong with that.<br /> <br /> The Southern Temple got the least text out of all, so they seem vague. However separate from the drugs and monotheism; they\u2019re basically alchemists with a sideline in Egyptian Myth. That\u2019s actually a niche that\u2019s unique in the official groups: \u201cHunting\u201d in order to learn from a spiritualistic direction. The NM and Net0 both hunt to learn but from a scientific direction.<br /> <br /> Finally the Jagged Crescent: These guys aren\u2019t (institutionally) religious or spiritual in the way the other two groups are. They don\u2019t even have community spirit, no matter how much they claim they do. The only things that reliably get them hunting monsters is protecting themselves or protecting the bottom line, but individuals may be more proactive. Though they also \u201chunt\u201d supplies, they\u2019re the ones in the Underworld collecting ingredients for U.<br /> <br /> <br /> So three groups, each with a clean non-muddled belief system (I\u2019d actually recommend against having mixed groups, cells are from one faction only). Any of them could be playable groups by themselves, but when you merge them together you create something far more interesting than the sum of its parts. You get cool things like a white rich kid who joined an occult society in collage going down to the projects; making the secret sign and all the locals glaring at him suddenly warm up. Or an improvised family is woman abducted by a Vampire, she gets a message out and it goes all the way to Egypt. None of the vampires know who the assassins were or how to strike back at them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, I think the Ascending Ones are the most conspiracy like of the Conspiracies. You have loads of independent groups of varying sizes that are all interconnected. You never know if some seemingly innocent group is connected to and protected by a vast conspiracy, and you can\u2019t strike back because it\u2019s too big to really care if you destroy the local chapter; and it\u2019s damn hard to trace the links between them. The other groups do, do conspiracy. An MM priest gives the nod to a guy in his congregation and a soldier leaves the base unlocked; but the vast nebulous web is unique to the Ascending Ones and I love that. I love how different the three groups are.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said I do think they really could use elaboration on how the groups look. Right now the Knife of Paradise can look a bit like The Long Night with Elixirs and more open minds. Talking about how they organise: Lone Cells of Ascending ones or lone cells of Tier 1 hunters who don\u2019t know about the Cult led by an Imam who does. City wide compacts between several cells. Hassassin like fortresses who send elite assassins where needed, when the local cell is outgunned or when there\u2019s a big advantage to not having any connections to the city where you hunt. Well that could make them be a bit more unique and flavourful.<br /> <br /> Same for the other groups. The Jagged Crescent for example consists of both international several drug cartels as well as neighbourhood sized gangs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway I\u2019ll stop here because this is getting stupidly long, but since I typed it I\u2019d like to know what you think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:08:14-08:00","id":4386,"title":"","content":"Oh, God. That damn VALKYRIE vampires bit is an eternal headache for me. I wish it had been a rumor, rather than &quot;here's the truth!&quot; Cheiron or the Panopticon would've both been welcome alternatives.<br /> <br /> Anyway. Your write-up has cleared things up a bit for me; their lack of well-defined, coherent organization is an asset. They are, in many ways, a group of organizations that all have a common goal, and can call upon each other, so that you never know just who could be one of them. I quite like that, and hadn't got that before.<br /> <br /> The niggling issue is the lack of central leadership. How exactly does each faction communicate, given their wildly differing motivations? It seems like any sort of large-scale or long-distance operation would be impossible for them. It almost seems like three unconnected Conspiracies that happen to share an Endowment. How do I bridge this gap and make them an organization?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T12:52:35-08:00","id":4531,"title":"","content":"Now central leadership is a legitimate issue. It's not nearly as bad as TF:V's Vampire but the description of how the Ascending ones are organised in Compacts and Conspiracies just doesn't work. There is no way that it would last as an organisation for 30 years, let alone 3000+ and it conflicts with earlier material even earlier in the same chapter. (Also, it has literally no redundancy!)<br /> <br /> So lets ignore that.<br /> <br /> The way I see it is that the Ascending Ones long distance organisation is powered by Elixirs. The AO are pretty much inspired by the myth of Hassassins, the myth that they uses drugs to induce visions of heaven, so I say that the Ascending Ones have an Elixir that lets them astrally project into heaven. What heaven really is (Temenos, the opposite to Inferno's Hell) doesn't matter right now. Since the Southern Temple most probably invented the Elixir and thus the whole system, Thoth's palace seems like a reasonable place to hold their meetings and central government. That gives them a secure central HQ that's always one Elixir away. That's how they organise global supply lines and call in the elite hunters if they need help.<br /> <br /> (In addition you probably have lots of local alliances. Sometimes you need to use the long distance network because the guys who can help you live on another continent; sometimes the guys on the other end of town are good enough.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T14:14:27-08:00","id":4583,"title":"","content":"I like to include the Cainite Heresy because it's a chance to make old game references through crazy babble. I really dig demons so the Lucifuge is probably my favorite. Combining the Lucifuge with the demon elements from Inferno made for a pretty good Hunter chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T17:59:50-08:00","id":4753,"title":"","content":"Compact: The Union. It's not about fighting for some over-mighty cause or to prevent the apocalypse, it's just about keeping your small corner of the world safe, which strikes a cord with a lot of people.<br /> <br /> Conspiracy: It's a toss-up between TFV and the Malleus. On the one hand, we've seen plenty of examples of Catholic hunters in the media, and we can easily see the possibilities of how to instantly turn a game on it's head when the friendly neighborhood priest breaks out his Mossberg, but TFV has the tech and the numbers.<br /> <br /> As for the vampire issue, I've said this before, so I'll include it here, it doesn't have to be &quot;TFV is controlled by the vampires&quot;. It can be, &quot;TFV and the vampires have to work together&quot;, &quot;TFV and another group that disguise themselves as vampires need to work together&quot;, or, &quot;TFV is pulling a massive double-blind to make people think it's vampires, meaning there's more hate directed at vampires than before.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T19:48:14-08:00","id":4796,"title":"","content":"Compact: Network Zero. I love that it's not hiding in the shadows but rather trying to expose them while trying to stay alive all the while.<br /> <br /> Conspiracy: Toss up between the VASCU and T:FV. I'm a 90's kid so these types of agencies tend to bring the xfiles fan out of me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T08:37:59-08:00","id":7367,"title":"","content":"Conspiracy: The Lucifuge. As others stated, I love the &quot;I'm supposed to be evil but I'm trying to do good&quot; sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Compact: The Union. I love the local feel and flavor of the group. Very realistic to me.<br /> <br /> I also love Ashwood Abbey, but that's only after I've had a number of alcoholic beverages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:12:18-08:00","id":7605,"title":"","content":"Huge TFV fan. Also, VASCU seems most like the oWoD FBI SAD. Lucifuge seems like a fun one, but if I ever do a Hunter game again it will have to me an X-Files/Warehouse 13/Fringe style deal, and those two are the best at that.<br /> <br /> Also, Cheiron Group is a fun one. For profit monster hunting rocks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T18:16:38-08:00","id":7786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3474-favorite-compacts-conspiracies?p=7605#post7605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huge TFV fan. Also, VASCU seems most like the oWoD FBI SAD. Lucifuge seems like a fun one, but if I ever do a Hunter game again it will have to me an X-Files/Warehouse 13/Fringe style deal, and those two are the best at that. Also, Cheiron Group is a fun one. For profit monster hunting rocks!</div> </div> </div> </div> Excellent taste. VASCU, TF:V, and Cheiron are my top three, because I love that real conspiracy take on things, a la X-Files or Fringe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T18:24:52-08:00","id":7793,"title":"","content":"Conspiracies: Knights of St George, easy. I like the Lucifuge next, but without some housefixes their powers are wildly unimpressive.<br /> Compacts: Ashwood Abbey, again easy. With the Promethean Brotherhood in second place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-10-2013, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T04:29:31-08:00","id":7972,"title":"","content":"While nor necessarily my favourites, I think that the Barrett Commission and the Talbot Group are highly under-appreciated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T03:24:18-08:00","id":10293,"title":"","content":"Conspiracy: Aegis Kai Doru is my biggest love affair in Hunter. Fantastic group, easy to use and brilliant setup as a conspiracy.<br /> Pretenders: Lucifuge. Who does not want to play enfants diabolique with a penchant for trying to make things better?<br /> <br /> <br /> Compact: Ashwood Abbey is maybe a bit too much to really play at times, but they make great antagonists for any other hunter group.<br /> <br /> Other interesting Hunters: Les mysteres and Promethean Brotherhood.<br /> <br /> As for the whole TF:V-Vampires: Im not a big TF:V fan. But if I were to play them I think the whole vampire-element in a certian book would be tossed away. same goes for the secret with Malleus as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T03:36:43-08:00","id":10297,"title":"","content":"I actually think the MM's secret was a far better idea than TF:Vs.<br /> <br /> Firstly, the MM haven't been subverted. Their leader might secretly be a Ghoul, but he's MM through and through. Secondly, I consider Ghouls to &quot;count as&quot; human. IMO if the morality trait is unchanged you're human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T05:43:11-08:00","id":10346,"title":"","content":"Conspiracies... tricky, but I'd say the Cheiron Group, the Malleus, and the Lucifuge (especially given the connections between the latter two). The Cheiron have that X-Files vibe by way of Gordon Gekko and American Psycho which I find incredibly interesting and fun, while the Lucifuge and MM have a certain resonance to them (you just can't beat the Inquisition for style). TFV and the Knights of St. George are fairly decent (I just ignore the vampire thing for TFV flat out), and none of the others much caught my attention.<br /> <br /> Compacts, probably the only very interesting ones to me are the Ashwood Abbey and the Loyalists of Thule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T08:11:55-08:00","id":10418,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=atamajakki;n4300I still dream of doing a game where VASCU and VALKYRIE reluctantly work together (the fact that they know about each other, and sometimes interact, is one of my favorite bits of canon) and are funded by Cheiron, rather than vampires. Maybe throw in Division Six. Play up the &quot;you can't trust your superiors&quot; angle. [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I was doing this in my Hunter game, Cheiron was funding their state government level compact. They were the guys in the white vans and trucks that dealt with all the dead monsters and ghouled cows. Was going to have them have to rescue a changeling ally from them and have to deal with the people they work with.<br /> <br /> I like Cheiron in that they are evil, but evil in a &quot;make money, ignore laws&quot; corporate evil not a whole Evil for evil sake like Pentax.<br /> <br /> Also live Network Zero for PCs and want to run a Werewolf game just to use the Talbot Group as antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T10:21:21-08:00","id":10541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3474-favorite-compacts-conspiracies?p=10297#post10297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> IMO if the morality trait is unchanged you're human.</div> </div> </div> </div>[pedantry]The Shuankhsen disagree.[/pedantry]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T10:52:26-08:00","id":10567,"title":"","content":"Compacts: The Thule. They are great mcguffins to throw at players but also their fun to play the group that walks up to the Darkness and say &quot;Whats all this then?&quot;<br /> <br /> Conspiracy: VASC/TFV. II'm a huge fan of Delta Green so when I look at these two and play in games with them, they're just two sides of the same coin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T18:02:47-08:00","id":13081,"title":"","content":"The fact the the US &quot;national security&quot; conspiracy is morally compromised by agreeing to work with some of its enemies against other enemies, while propping up the former enemies, and keeps the lower ranked people in the dark on that - is really really really on theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T02:05:06-08:00","id":13280,"title":"","content":"It is; but putting some of those enemies in charge is not.<br /> <br /> US black ops are morally compromised by their dirty deals, but I can't remember anything in reality or in spy fiction where it turns out a middle eastern dictator propped up by the CIA ended up usurping the CIA from the US government.<br /> <br /> It would be far more in theme for the vampires to be metaphorically Afghanistan than the Illuminati.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T08:11:55-08:00","id":14053,"title":"","content":"I've always been a huge fan of the Loyalists of Thule, my favorite sorts of characters are the ones who are dangerous for the simple fact that they just know a little too much for their own good and are just a little too clever for everyone else's. When I'm running games I actually have a slight preference for union NPCs, both because their motivations are very relatable and because when demonic forces take over a shopping mall nobody expects the janitor to be the one who takes charge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T13:40:52-08:00","id":14261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3474-favorite-compacts-conspiracies?p=10297#post10297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. IMO if the morality trait is unchanged you're human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Purified: &quot;Why everyone just keep forgetting about me? Especially since those those hipster* &quot;arisen&quot; mummies showed up..&quot;<br /> <br /> *hipsters in &quot;we-were-mummies-before-you-even-thought-we-were-invented-later&quot; kind of way","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T04:16:50-08:00","id":37784,"title":"","content":"Compact: <b>The Night Watch</b> (<u>Street Angel</u>) =Prefering to Patrol the Streets, Dark Alleyways and Midnight Subway trains and Bus routes. It makes sense that Monsters, Psycho's and everything in-between would hide in areas that most of society including cops would avoid or just take a blind eye too. The <u>Union </u>can be considered the same in some cases. (( But they come off like a bunch of rallying Hicks, the kind you see in movies with pitchforks and torches filled with anger and paranoia or maybe they just need a reason to shoot their guns. ))<br /> <br /> <b> Talbot Group</b> (<u>Conciliators</u>)= It's fun sometimes to play the redeemer, also to rub elbows/helping the werewolves &amp; spirits can lead to a lot of interesting if not dangerous adventures with dark spirits, raging werewolves or other changing breeds and Hunter cells with a low tolerance for compassion or understanding the paranormal.<br /> <br /> Conspiracy: '<b>Ascending Ones</b> ( <u>Knife of Paradise</u>)= They feel like the best and only sect. in this group i can get behind in my opinion. There not as dogmatic and also open-minded as a whole. While keeping innocents safe and unaware of the dark creatures around them. I also like the whole Elixir method they use to face their enemies. <b>VASCU</b> (<u> Field Liaison Department</u>)= To be honest i like all the sects. to this hunter group, being my Favorite Conspiracy if not Hunter Group of all. Loving &quot;X-Files&quot;, and the games such as &quot;Condemned&quot; and &quot;Deadly Premonition&quot; certainly have something to do with it. Aside from having psychic abilities that gives an edge to there investigations, they also join &amp; watch other hunter cells. Giving aid or just keeping an eye on them if there methods go too far &quot; Unless your <u>TF:V&quot;</u>. They aim to capture killer monsters and human alike. So you can really do a lot with this group. ((I like these guys over <u>TF:V</u> cause they seem to come off more Sociable Detective style that seems to have to cooperate with local law enforcement as well as other hunters to some degree or another.<u> Team Force Valkyrie </u>feels like a Paranormal Black Op group of labdogs, that would commandeer or take over any hunter operation because &quot;Government&quot;, without having to answer to anybody. But they can take you away and others that the govt. may assume to be a threat. Not really helping people as so much. &quot;just following orders so get out of our wa.y&quot; Not to say they can't be played as hero's, and valiant soilders, but.. they just came off a little too &quot;Big Brother/Jackboot thugs&quot; when i first read about them. Just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}